instructions.out:
Score this sales conversation with BANT. For each part give the points of the rubric line that the conversation supports; with no evidence, give 0. Do not guess in the customer's favour.
RUBRIC (points → meaning):
{
 "budget": {
  "3": "budget confirmed and sufficient for the scope",
  "1": "a budget exists, size unknown",
  "0": "no budget yet, must request it internally",
  "disqualify": "explicitly looking for free or very cheap alternatives"
 },
 "authority": {
  "3": "direct decision-maker",
  "2": "strong influencer with a named decision-maker",
  "0": "researcher without access to the decision-maker"
 },
 "need": {
  "3": "a clear, urgent, specific problem our products solve",
  "1": "general interest, no specific pain",
  "0": "vague, or outside what we offer"
 },
 "timeline": {
  "3": "live within 30 days",
  "2": "30 to 90 days",
  "1": "90 to 180 days",
  "0": "no timeline, exploratory"
 }
}
COMPANY FIT red flags: ["wants capabilities beyond our products without a custom project", "expects prices far below our floor margin", "a known payment default", "a geography with export-control or compliance issues", "fishing for our methods without purchase intent"]
COMPANY FIT green flags: ["has bought similar solutions before", "has a team able to adopt and maintain it", "a use case in an industry we already serve"]
Name only flags the conversation shows. disqualify: true only for the rubric's disqualify case or a clear red flag.
intent: what the customer's LAST message asks for: question (about a product or the company), price (asks what something costs), quotation (asks for a formal quotation), detailed (describes a project, site or requirements in detail, or a tender/RFP), meeting (asks for a call or demo), slot_pick (answers which offered meeting time suits them), accept (accepts a quotation or says they will order), reject (declines), objection (pushes back on price, timing or terms), other.
product: the product family the conversation is about. rationale: two sentences, plain.
